{"header":"<h1>Module type <code><span>Domains_intf.EntryNotation</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"alt-ergo-lib","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"AltErgoLib","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Domains_intf","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"EntryNotation","href":"#","kind":"module-type"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-entry\"><a href=\"#type-entry\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> entry</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The type of entries that hold a mutable reference to a domain.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-domain\"><a href=\"#type-domain\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> domain</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>The type of domains.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-(!!)\"><a href=\"#val-(!!)\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> (!!) : <span><a href=\"#type-entry\">entry</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"#type-domain\">domain</a></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Return the domain associated with this entry.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-update\"><a href=\"#val-update\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> update : <span><span class=\"label\">ex</span>:<a href=\"../../Explanation/index.html#type-t\">Explanation.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"#type-entry\">entry</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><a href=\"#type-domain\">domain</a> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> unit</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>update ~ex e d</code> updates the domain associated with <code>e</code>, intersecting it with <code>d</code>. The explanation <code>ex</code> is added to <code>d</code>.</p><ul class=\"at-tags\"><li class=\"raises\"><span class=\"at-tag\">raises</span> <a href=\"../module-type-Domain/index.html#exception-Inconsistent\"><code>Domain.Inconsistent</code></a> <p>if the domains are incompatible.</p></li></ul></div></div>"}